{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016mFpyCsYcXUkkNfaDrcDHE","type":"tool_result","content":"**D25 \"Hive Mind\" = REGISTRY HIVE** (`registry.hive_root_name` of one `hive-001.hiv`, 8192 B = 4 KiB base block +\none 4 KiB hbin; id `d25-registry-001-registry-hive-root-name`, `exact_text`/`trim`). Answer = the ROOT nk cell's name\nverbatim (base block u32 @0x24 -> cell 0x1000+off -> `nk`, name len u16 @nk+0x48, name @nk+0x4c, ASCII when flag\n0x20). DECOY: base-block FileName UTF-16 @0x30 (\"renamed\": single = truncated kebab path of the root name, timed =\nunrelated `<word>-<8hex>.hiv`). fmt word is the DOMAIN `registry`, not `regf` -> race MISS (lib had\n`regf.root_key_name`), live worker ~17 s, 0 wrong; TT 30 / Mastery 270 (NINE sets) first try, 2-3 s. Every D25 hive:\nseq1 == seq2, v1.3, root @0x20, flags 0x2c, 0 subkeys, 2 root values `Marker` (REG_SZ, single\n`HUNTRESS-HIVE-4203`, timed random hex) + `Ordinal` (REG_DWORD inline, 4203 = the marker's number) -- the unasked\n\"host labels\" for \"regroup the systems, and isolate the planted hive\".\n**D26 \"Before You Go\" = WINDOWS PREFETCH** (`prefetch.executable_name` of one `trace-001.pf`; id\n`d26-prefetch-001-prefetch-executable-name`, `exact_text`/`trim`). Single = `MAM\\x04` Xpress-Huffman-compressed (3896 B\n-> SCCA v30); TT + all 10 Mastery sets = UNCOMPRESSED SCCA v30 (~15.3 KB). Answer = SCCA header exe name UTF-16LE @16\nto the first NUL, verbatim uppercase with `.EXE` (`CMD.EXE`, `PACKAGER.EXE`, `GLACIER96.EXE`); the `.pf` filename is\nrenamed (`trace-001.pf`, no `NAME-HASH`). The D16-night prebuild `prefetch` (pure-Python MS-XCA decoder) HIT: CORRECT\n~29 s, 0 wrong; TT 31 / Mastery 310 (TEN sets) first try. `dissect.util` (lzxpress_huffman) IS installed in .venv\n(worker cross-check). Flavor (unasked): \"even after filenames changed ... connect execution traces to the correct\nhosts\" -> siblings: header name vs filename stem / path hash, volume serial + device path + volume creation time\n(= host), the full exe path from the filename strings.\n**D27 \"Packet Loss Prevention\" = PCAP** (`pcap.packet_count` of one `capture-001.pcap`, 119 B: classic libpcap LE-us\n`d4 c3 b2 a1` v2.4, snaplen 65535, linktype 147 USER0, 3 records; id `d27-pcap-001-pcap-packet-count`, `integer`/\n`trim`). Count = 24-B global header, then 16-B record headers advancing by incl_len u32 @+8 until EOF. The D16-night\nprebuild `pcap.py` HIT the race (CORRECT ~22 s, 0 wrong); TT 32 / Mastery 352 (ELEVEN sets, 5.8 s) first try. Timed\npcaps mutated inside the classic format only: magic LE-us / LE-ns `4d 3c b2 a1` / BE-us `a1 b2 c3 d4` (3 of 11 sets\nbig-endian), linktype 1/101/105/147, snaplen 256-262144, 3-39 records, some snapped (incl_len < orig_len, still\ncounted); no pcapng, no truncated tail. Synthesis grew to SIX names (note/png/msi/wav/jar/pcap). Flavor (unasked):\n\"Packet captures, exports, and host artifacts describe the same incident from different angles. Count traffic,\nreject malformed captures, and find the host narrative missing network evidence.\" -> siblings: malformed-capture\ndetection (truncated record, incl_len > snaplen, bad version), flow/log EXPORTS (Zeek, NetFlow, CSV) whose count\ndiffers, HOST artifacts (Sysmon EID 3/22, firewall log, netstat) claiming a connection the capture lacks.\n**D28 \"Where It All Began\" = RAW GPT DISK IMAGE** (`disk.partition_start_lba_sequence` of one `disk-001.img`, 131 072\nB = 256 x 512-B sectors; id `d28-disk-001-disk-partition-start-lba-sequence`, kind `json` \"compact valid JSON array\nwith exact values and order\", norm `trim`). Protective MBR (`ee`) + `EFI PART` @LBA1 (rev 1.0, CRCs valid), entry\narray @LBA2 128 x 128 B, backup header at the last LBA; answer = first LBA u64 @entry+32 of every used entry in TABLE\norder as JSON integers (single `[34]`; timed 1-6 partitions, starts 34-367, table order == ascending in all 14\nimages). Race MISS: `vbr.py` had the GPT walk under fmts `gpt`/`mbr`/`partition_table` (`partition_start_lbas`), and\nlib's `disk` fmt (disk.py) = VHD/VHDX/VMDK/QCOW2 detection only -> live worker, CORRECT ~22 s, 0 wrong; TT 33 /\nMastery 396 (TWELVE sets) first try, 3-4 s. Partitions were ALL ZERO (no filesystem, no carved evidence) in every\nmode. Flavor (unasked): \"Disk images hold every previous artifact family in context. Recover partition layouts,\nlocate evidence by offset, and prove which image was rebuilt from an incomplete source.\" -> siblings: partition\nend/size/name/type-GUID sequences, byte offsets, earlier families embedded inside partitions (find by magic -> LBA /\noffset / partition index), primary-vs-backup GPT + CRC + truncated-image checks (\"rebuilt from incomplete source\"),\nmulti-image comparison.\n**D29 \"Trust Issues\" = X.509 CERTIFICATE** (`x509.sha256_fingerprint` of one `certificate-001.pem`, 709 B, one LF\nPEM block, Ed25519; id `d29-x509-001-x509-sha256-fingerprint`, `pattern` 64 hex, `case_insensitive`). Answer = sha256 of\nthe DER (decoded base64 body). The D16-night prebuild `x509.py` HIT the race (CORRECT ~23 s, 0 wrong); TT 34 / Mastery\n442 (13 sets) first try; all 15 timed certs the same shape. Flavor (unasked): \"Certificates appear in binaries,\npackages, mail, captures, and disk images. Fingerprint each one, collapse duplicates, and identify the trust claim\nunsupported by evidence.\" -> siblings: certs inside PE Authenticode / APK signing / eml S/MIME / pcap TLS / disk\nimages, dedup by fingerprint across containers, issuer-without-matching-CA or signature that does not verify.\n**D30 \"Seeing Double\" = CORPUS RELATIONS** (`relation.identical_sha256_groups` of `cluster-001.zip`; id\n`d30-cluster-001-relation-identical-sha256-groups` -- id family `cluster`, fmt `relation`; kind `json`,\n`case_insensitive`). The FIRST field about relationships BETWEEN members rather than one member's struct. Single:\n`delivery-manifest.json` (`huntress.artifact_delivery_manifest.v1`: id/filename/path/content_type/family/producer_id/\nsize_bytes/sha256; copies `producer_id: duplicate_ref`) + 30 `artifacts/<id>.<ext>` (txt/ps1/json/png/zip) = 5 exact\ngroups x 6; answer = groups of manifest `id`s (zip paths and basenames REJECTED). Timed (15 clusters): NO manifest,\nextensionless `artifacts/<word>-NN`, shuffled CD, 19-32 members, 2-5 exact groups of 2-6, singletons, one 1-2-byte\nNEAR-duplicate shadowing each group, inner zips (one `.txt` each) of which one per group has a BAD CRC. No `relation`\nfmt in lib -> race MISS, live CORRECT ~88 s with 3 wrong (label spelling + an empty submit); TT 35 / Mastery 490 (14\nsets) first try. Flavor (unasked): \"Build a relationship map from exact identity, semantic identity, containment, and\nclaimed provenance -- then expose the fabricated cluster.\" -> the four unasked relation kinds + the fabricated\nmember/cluster are physically present in the timed bytes.\nProgression: D19-D22 runnable formats -> D23 APPLICATION DATA -> D24-D26 WINDOWS DFIR -> D27 NETWORK -> D28 DISK -> D29\nTRUST (certs) -> D30 CORPUS RELATIONS (dedup across a member set). D31 is the LAST day: a finale most plausibly asks\nthe next `relation.*` kind on a cluster (semantic identity, containment, claimed-provenance mismatch, near-duplicate /\n\"fabricated\" member, or the fabricated cluster among several) or a cross-family corpus question (inventory by magic,\nextension liars, cert dedup across containers). D31 timed kits will carry `relation.identical_sha256_groups` with\nmutations (manifest present/absent, nested dirs, md5/sha1/size variants, more near-dups). Single-member families are\nall built; the relation layer is the readiness gap.\n\n## 1. Atlas","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e49d64d-65c0-4a5a-ab5e-a623d76a2cdc","uuid":"29053532-cecc-4739-9bb6-8b5a2db317e2","timestamp":"2026-10-31T04:36:53.849Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"**D25 \"Hive Mind\" = REGISTRY HIVE** (`registry.hive_root_name` of one `hive-001.hiv`, 8192 B =