le worker pre-wired the dispatch -> TT 23 / Mastery 115 CORRECT in-window first try. D19: Files = note + document-001.pdf + shortcut-001.lnk + collector-001.elf; the single worker added an ELF extractor but NOT the synthesis branch -> TT and Mastery solver_incomplete -> offline generalize ported D18's branch. 4 of 5 timed days lost this way: the day's solver must start from the previous day's solve.py. D21: Files grew to FIVE names (note + panel png + managed dll + message eml + mobile-001.apk), same list in all 5 Mastery sets, order re-rolled per set -- never assume a count. D22-D23: Files = FIVE names and DIFFER between sets of one Mastery (D23: note/panel png/msi/mp4/sqlite vs note/pdf/lnk/mp4/sqlite) -- parse each set's text; still sha256-only. D24: FIVE names (note + document-001.pdf + collector-001.elf + shortcut-001.lnk + events-001.evtx), same five in all 8 Mastery sets, order re-rolled; sha256 only. D25: still sha256 order over 5 names (note/pdf/elf/lnk/hiv, or note/macos/docx/zip/hiv), per-set lists differ. D26: still sha256 + FIVE names (note + {evidence-drop-001.zip | document-001.pdf} + document-15-001.docx + macos-001.bin + trace-001.pf), pdf/zip swapped between Mastery sets; Mastery identity ids also differ per set (7 of 21 asked). D27: SIX names (note/png/msi/wav/jar/pcap, order shuffled per set) in TT and all 11 Mastery sets, still sha256 -- the list length grows; parse it, never count it. D30: the lane's first CORPUS field `relation.identical_sha256_groups` (cluster-001.zip, groups of member ids by real sha256) -- a grouping, not an order; it rides beside the digest-order synthesis in the D30 kits (TT 35 / Mastery 14 sets first try). Relation siblings are tracked as relation-* gaps.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"timed-carryover-mutations\", \"concept\": \"Timed kits mutate every carried family; json lists must be SORTED\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D23 TT/Mastery re-rolled values that were constant D13-D22: PE Machine 0x01c0/0x01c2/0x01c4/0x01f0/0x0ebc/0x5064/0x8664, ELF e_machine 0x0003/0x0028/0x002b/0x0102, audio mp3/opus/vorbis/pcm_s16le, video dims arbitrary, Mach-O FAT 2-3 slices (0x7, 0xc, 0x12, 0x01000007, 0x0100000c, 0x01000012, 0x0200000c), shuffled zip CD, PDF 1.0-2.0, BOM true, identity sizes 72-378 B, sqlite page 512-65536. lib answered all values right; the two failures were list ORDER: GM wants zip CD names and macho cpu_type_set SORTED ascending (CD order rejected; fat_arch order != accepted) and a local override returned a Python list -> repr. Action for lib/solver owners: one json choke point (sorted + compact) for every `json` answer except `*-synthesis-*-order`; fixture tests with multi-slice fat, shuffled CD, Ogg Opus/Vorbis, MP3, non-x86 PE/ELF so the next carried family (sqlite) is covered for its mutations too (page size 1 = 65536, WAL header, UTF-16 encodings). D24: the D23 fixes held -- TT 29 / Mastery 232 (8 sets) first try while the kit mutated again: audio `ftyp M4A ` -> aac and `fLaC` -> flac (still named audio-001.wav), Mach-O thin LE-32 `ce fa ed fe` (60 B) -> [\\\"0x0000000c\\\"] beside fat 2-3 slices, PE 0x0266 MIPS16, ELF 0x0016 S390 / 0x00b7 AArch64 / 0x00f3 RISC-V, SQLite page 2048, PDF 1.1/1.6/1.7. Expect EVTX to mutate from D25: several chunks, record-id gaps, a dirty header, an empty or zeroed second chunk -- the record_count walk must cover every chunk. D25 (TT 30 / Mastery 270 = 9 sets) all first try with zero generalize: carried extractors held; identity names carry a random `-<6hex>` suffix (ids keep the bare stem), 2 of 9 Mastery sets used a different kit (macos/docx/inner zip, no roster). From D26 the kit carries `d25-registry-001-registry-hive-root-name`: parse root offset @0x24 generally (root not at 0x20, multiple hbins, UTF-16 name when nk flag 0x20 is clear, non-ASCII latin-1 names). D26: TT 31 / Mastery 310 (10 sets) first try; the NEW family's wrapper flipped between modes (single MAM\\\\x04-compressed prefetch, every timed .pf plain SCCA v30) -- branch on magic, never on mode. Expect D27+ timed kits to mutate prefetch (other SCCA versions 17/23/26/31, MAM with CRC, compressed in timed) and registry (root cell not @0x20, UTF-16 root names) -- see prefetch-carryover-variants. D27: TT 32 / Mastery 352 (11 sets) first try with zero generalize; the new pcap family already mutated within classic libpcap in the timed sets (LE-us, LE-ns 4d3cb2a1, BE a1b2c3d4; linktypes 1/101/105/147; snapped records). From D28 the kit carries d27-pcap-001-pcap-packet-count -- see pcap-carryover-variants. D29 certs did not mutate (15 one-block LF Ed25519 PEMs). D30 cluster: single had a manifest + extensions, timed had NO manifest, extensionless shuffled names, near-duplicates and bad-CRC inner zips -> D31 may flip any of these (manifest back, nested dirs, md5/size groups); hash members as blobs, read raw on bad CRC.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"relation-identical-groups-variants\", \"concept\": \"`relation.*` exact-identity siblings of D30's identical_sha256_groups on a corpus zip (other hash, size, aggregates, label shapes)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt relation (aliases corpus, cluster, dedup, inventory), member = a cluster zip (`cluster-NNN.zip`, optional `delivery-manifest.json` / any `*manifest*.json` / index.json). Fields: identical_sha256_groups (D30 GM-CONFIRMED: groups len>=2 of member labels, each sorted, groups sorted, compact JSON), identical_md5_groups, identical_sha1_groups, identical_sha512_groups, identical_size_groups, duplicate_groups, unique_sha256_count, duplicate_group_count, duplicate_member_count (members in groups minus one per group AND total, register both as _redundant/_in_groups), largest_group_size, singleton_ids, member_count. Label rule: manifest `id` mapped by `path` then `filename`; no manifest -> basename without extension (D30 timed `artifacts/<word>-NN`). Skip the manifest itself and directory entries; recurse into `artifacts/` subdirs; hash members as raw blobs (inner zips may hold bad-CRC entries; outer read falls back to a raw local-header read). Cache per (container sha256), never id().\"},\n  {\"id\": \"relation-near-duplicate-fabricated\", \"concept\": \"Near-duplicate / fabricated members of a corpus: a 1-2-byte edit of an exact group's content, archives whose stored CRC does not match\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt relation. D30 timed clusters (all 15) held, beside each exact group, ONE member equal in size differing in 1-2 bytes (`$ErrorActionPrfference`) and inner zips with one `.txt` where one copy has a stored CRC32 != data CRC (zipfile raises BadZipFile). Fields: near_duplicate_groups (group label list incl. the near-copy? register both: near_duplicate_ids = only the non-exact members, near_duplicate_pairs = [[exact_rep, near]] sorted), fabricated_ids, fabricated_member(s), crc_mismatch_ids / bad_crc_member_ids, corrupted_ids, tampered_ids, modified_copy_ids. Algorithm: for every non-grouped member, compare against each group's content: same length and Hamming distance <=4, or Levenshtein <=4 for small files (<4 KiB), or same zip member names with different data; CRC check = zlib.crc32(raw-decompressed) vs CD crc. Output sorted labels, compact JSON.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"relation-semantic-identity-groups\", \"concept\": \"Semantic identity groups: members equal after format-aware normalization (the D30 flavor's 'semantic identity')\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt relation. Fields: semantic_identity_groups, semantically_identical_groups, normalized_content_groups, canonical_json_groups, normalized_text_groups, pixel_identical_groups, same_content_different_hash_groups (= semantic groups that are NOT exact groups). Canonical key per family by MAGIC: text/ps1/csv -> strip UTF-8/16 BOM, decode, CRLF/CR->LF, rstrip each line, strip trailing newlines (keep case); JSON -> json.loads then dumps(sort_keys, compact); PNG -> IHDR + zlib-decompressed concatenated IDAT (ignore tEXt/tIME/iTXt and chunk order); JPEG -> bytes from SOS to EOI (ignore APPn/COM); zip -> sorted (name, sha256(data)) ignoring timestamps/extra/comment/order; gzip -> decompressed payload. Group len>=2, labels as relation-identical-groups-variants. Stdlib only (zlib, json).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"relation-containment-map\", \"concept\": \"Containment relations in a corpus: which archive members contain which other members (by hash)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt relation. Fields: containment_pairs ([[container_label, contained_label_or_inner_name]] sorted), contained_ids (corpus members whose sha256 appears inside another member), container_ids, nested_member_names, nested_sha256s, max_nesting_depth, orphan_inner_members (inner contents matching no corpus member). D30 timed: inner zips each hold ONE `<word>.txt` (29-97 B) whose bytes matched NO other cluster member in sampled sets -- so also answer by inner name. Walk zip (raw-read on bad CRC: local header @offset, skip 30+n+e, inflate -15), gzip, tar; recurse <=3 levels; label inner entries `<container_label>/<inner name>` only if the field asks names.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"relation-claimed-provenance\", \"concept\": \"Claimed provenance vs evidence: delivery-manifest claims (sha256, size, content_type, family, producer_id/duplicate_ref) checked against the real bytes\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt relation. Manifest schema seen D30: `{schema: huntress.artifact_delivery_manifest.v1, artifacts: [{id, filename, path, content_type, family, producer_id (text_template|structured_image|structured_zip|duplicate_ref), size_bytes, sha256}]}` -- in D30 every claim was TRUE (single), timed had no manifest. Fields: claimed_hash_mismatch_ids, sha256_claim_mismatch_ids, size_claim_mismatch_ids, content_type_mismatch_ids (claim vs magic: text/plain, application/json, image/png, application/zip), family_mismatch_ids, unsupported_duplicate_ref_ids (producer duplicate_ref whose bytes match no original), missing_member_ids (claimed but absent), unlisted_member_names (present but unclaimed), provenance_mismatch_ids (union), fabricated_ids. Sorted labels, compact JSON; `[]` when all claims hold.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"relation-multi-cluster-fabricated\", \"concept\": \"Expose the fabricated cluster: several cluster-NNN.zip members, pick the one whose relations/claims do not hold\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt relation; question may target the evidence zip or each cluster. Fields: fabricated_cluster (filename), fabricated_cluster_id, cluster_with_claim_mismatches, clusters_sharing_content_groups, cross_cluster_identical_groups ([[\\\"cluster-001/alpha-01\\\",...]]). Score each cluster: manifest claim mismatches, near-dups, bad CRC entries, members identical to another cluster's members, timestamps in the future / identical DOS times across 'independent' sources. Return the single max-score cluster name verbatim (with .zip) and register a stem variant.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"relation-corpus-family-inventory\", \"concept\": \"Finale-style corpus inventory over every earlier family: per-member family by MAGIC, extension liars, counts\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt relation (aliases corpus, inventory). Fields: family_by_magic (JSON object or sorted [[label, family]] -- register both), family_counts, extension_mismatch_ids (extension vs magic), magic_family_set (sorted list of families present), members_by_family_<fam>, largest_member_id, total_bytes. Reuse lib's magic sniffer (PE/ELF/Mach-O/CFB/PK subtypes APK/JAR/OOXML/zip, PDF, PNG, JPEG, SQLite, EVTX, regf, SCCA/MAM, pcap, GPT image, PEM/DER cert, text/json/ps1). Family words = the lane's GM fmt words (email, media, registry, disk, x509, pe, elf, macho, apk, jar, sqlite, evtx, prefetch, pcap, pdf, png, jpeg, zip, ooxml, msi, lnk).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"gate-allowlist-dfir-libs\", \"concept\": \"Prebuild gate refuses installed DFIR libs\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"hctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS lacks Evtx, regipy, olefile, oletools, dnfile, LnkParse3, lief, cryptography, asn1crypto, dpkt, PIL, sqlite3, wave, ordlookup. Targets evtx-records (python-evtx) and regf-values (regipy) as written will fail the gate exactly like pe-debug-rich-imports did (import ordlookup). Either widen the allowlist (all are in .venv) or rewrite those goals as stdlib/struct parsers. Also `open` is banned: regipy RegistryHive needs a path -> use a struct nk/vk walker.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"disk-partition-fields\", \"concept\": \"`disk.*` partition-layout siblings of D28's start-LBA sequence on RAW images (fmt word collision fix)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Extend lib/meta/prebuilt/disk.py (or a new disk_layout.py registered under fmt disk + aliases image, raw_disk, disk_image, dd, gpt, mbr, partition_table): when no VHD/VHDX/VMDK/QCOW2 magic matches, parse the raw image -- GPT if MBR slot type 0xEE and `EFI PART` at LBA1 (probe 512 then 4096-B sectors), else MBR (4 x 16 B @0x1BE, EBR chain for 05/0f/85: logical start = EBR LBA + rel, next EBR = extended start + rel). Read entry LBA/count/size from the header (u64 @+72, u32 @+80, u32 @+84), skip zero type-GUID entries. GM-confirmed D28: partition_start_lba_sequence = JSON ints, TABLE order (compact). Siblings, all TABLE order, compact JSON: partition_end_lba_sequence / partition_last_lba_sequence (GPT last LBA inclusive; MBR start+count-1), partition_sector_count_sequence (end-start+1), partition_size_bytes_sequence (x sector size), partition_start_offset_bytes_sequence (start x sector size), partition_name_sequence (GPT UTF-16LE @+56, 72 B, to NUL), partition_type_guid_sequence (mixed-endian -> lowercase canonical), partition_unique_guid_sequence, partition_type_sequence (MBR `0x%02x`), partition_attributes_u64_hex_sequence; scalars partition_count, partition_table_type (`gpt`/`dos` as sfdisk prints `label:`), disk_guid (lowercase canonical), disk_signature_u32_hex (MBR @0x1B8), sector_size_bytes, first_usable_lba, last_usable_lba, alternate_lba / backup_header_lba, partition_entry_lba, partition_entry_count, partition_entry_size_bytes, image_size_bytes, image_sector_count, largest_partition_index (0-based table slot) / name. Also accept the field without `_sequence` (plural `s`, `_list`). Fixtures: build GPT images with 1-6 entries, an MBR+EBR image, a 4Kn GPT. Never sort -- `_sequence` = table order.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"disk-carryover-variants\", \"concept\": \"disk-001.img as a CARRIED timed family: every shape D29+ kits may mutate it into\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D23-D27 showed every carried family mutates in TT/Mastery the day after it is introduced. Harden the partition walk (#180, disk-partition-fields) and keep start_lba_sequence correct for: MBR-only `dos` images (no 0xEE), extended + logical partitions (EBR chain, type 05/0f/85, loops guarded), hybrid MBR (0xEE + real entries -> GPT wins), 4096-B sector GPT (`EFI PART` @4096; LBAs stay in 4K sectors), non-contiguous used entries (empty slots between -> skip, keep table order), entries whose table order != LBA order (emit table order), entry_size 256 / entry count != 128, damaged primary header (bad CRC or zeroed LBA1) -> read the BACKUP header at the last LBA (its entry array sits before it), image truncated before the backup, GPT inside a VHD fixed footer / VMDK monolithicFlat / qcow2 (unwrap first), gzip/xz-compressed `.img.gz`. Fixture every case; one sample per shape in the prebuild gate.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"disk-evidence-by-offset\", \"concept\": \"'Locate evidence by offset': earlier-family members embedded in a disk image\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D28 flavor: 'Disk images hold every previous artifact family in context ... locate evidence by offset'. New module lib/meta/prebuilt/disk_carve.py, fmt disk (aliases image, evidence): scan the image for every family magic the lane has seen (PNG 89504e47, JPEG ffd8ff, %PDF-, PK0304, MZ+PE, 7f454c46, cffaedfe/cafebabe, d0cf11e0, 4c000000+CLSID, `SQLite format 3`, ElfFile, regf, SCCA@4 / MAM, pcap magics, OggS/RIFF/ftyp), preferring sector-aligned hits, and also map files through a FAT/NTFS/ext filesystem if one exists. Fields: evidence_offset_bytes / <family>_offset_bytes (decimal), evidence_lba / <family>_start_lba, evidence_partition_index (0-based table slot; also 1-based `_number`), evidence_offset_in_partition_bytes, embedded_family_sequence (families in offset order, lane fmt words `png` `pdf` `pe` ...), embedded_member_count, evidence_sha256 (carve by the format's own length: PNG IEND, zip EOCD, PE SizeOfImage/last section, SQLite page_size x page_count, EVTX chunks, regf hbins size, pcap record walk). Question may name the evidence by its old member name (`panel-001.png`) -> match by magic + family.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"disk-rebuilt-integrity\", \"concept\": \"'Prove which image was rebuilt from an incomplete source': GPT/MBR consistency and truncation checks\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"New module lib/meta/prebuilt/disk_integrity.py, fmt disk (aliases gpt, image). Fields (enum true|false unless noted): primary_header_crc_valid (CRC32 of hdr_size bytes with @+16 zeroed), partition_array_crc_valid (CRC32 of count x size @entry LBA vs @+88), backup_header_present (`EFI PART` at the last LBA AND at alternate_lba), backup_matches_primary (same disk GUID/entries/usable range; my_lba/alternate swapped), alternate_lba_matches_image_end, image_truncated (alternate_lba or any partition last LBA >= image sector count), partitions_beyond_image_count, protective_mbr_size_matches (0xEE count = min(sectors-1, 0xFFFFFFFF)), overlapping_partitions, zero_filled_partition_sequence / empty_partition_count, header_crc32_u32_hex / partition_array_crc32_u32_hex (`0x%08x` stored and computed), integrity_status / rebuilt_indicator enum (`intact`, `rebuilt`, `truncated`, `crc_mismatch` -- unverified spelling, also emit the booleans). Multi-image synthesis: 'which image was rebuilt' = the image whose backup/CRC/size claims are inconsistent; answer its member filename.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"disk-image-synthesis\", \"concept\": \"Cross-image synthesis over several disk-NNN.img members (and the D15+ digest-order synthesis carrying a large .img)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Extend lib/meta/prebuilt/synthesis*.py: ids `metadata-day-NN-synthesis-<key>-order|groups|<x>` with Files listing disk images: order by partition_count / first start LBA / image size / disk GUID, group images by identical partition layout (same start/end sequence), 'rebuilt image' = the one failing disk-rebuilt-integrity or whose layout matches another but whose partition contents are zero/truncated, partition-content sha256 per image (hash each partition's byte range: partition_sha256_sequence). D28 synthesis already hashed a multi-100-KB `.img` in-window; keep per-set byte caching (no id()-keyed caches, D25).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"filesystem-in-partition-walk\", \"concept\": \"The layer inside a partition: filesystem directory walk -> file names, sizes, start cluster, byte offset\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"New module lib/meta/prebuilt/fs_walk.py, fmts fat (aliases fat12, fat16, fat32, vfat), exfat, ntfs, ext (aliases ext2, ext3, ext4), filesystem, disk (partition-relative: accept `partition_N_` / `pN_` prefixes, default first partition). Reuse vbr.py for the boot sector. FAT: root dir (FAT12/16 fixed region; FAT32 root cluster @0x2C), 32-B dirents + LFN (0x0F) reassembly, deleted 0xE5, cluster chain via FAT -> file_names (sorted), file_count, volume_label (dirent attr 0x08), <file>_start_cluster, <file>_offset_bytes (image-absolute = part_lba*ss + data_region + (clus-2)*cluster_size), <file>_size_bytes, created/modified times (DOS local -> `YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS`). exFAT: 0x85/0xC0/0xC1 entry sets, label 0x83. NTFS: $MFT at mft_cluster*cluster -> FILE records (fixups) -> $FN names, $DATA resident/non-resident first run -> offset. ext4: superblock @1024 (`53 ef` @0x38): volume_name @0x78, uuid @0x68, last_mounted @0x88, block size, inode 2 root dir (extents 0xF30A or block map) -> names. Cross-check with TSK `fls -o <lba> f.img` / `icat` / `fsstat` (installed, worker-only).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"prefetch-carryover-variants\", \"concept\": \"Prefetch as a CARRIED timed family: every SCCA version and MAM wrapper the kit may mutate into\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D26 single was MAM\\\\x04-compressed, timed plain SCCA v30 -- the wrapper flips between modes, so D27+ timed kits will likely mutate `trace-001.pf`. fmt prefetch (aliases pf, scca), keep every existing field name and make it version-general: v17 (XP/2003: file info 68 B @84, last run FILETIME @0x78, run count @0x90), v23 (Vista/7: last run @0x80, run count @0x98), v26 (8.1: 8 last runs @0x80, run count @0xD0), v30 BOTH layouts (220-B file info: run count @0xD0; 212-B 'variant 2': @0xC8 -- pick by metrics array offset @84 = 0x130 vs 0x128), v31 (Win11 24H2+: parse as v30, choose layout the same way) and an unknown version (still answer executable_name / prefetch_hash / file_size from the fixed header). MAM wrapper: type low nibble 4 = Xpress-Huffman with and without CRC flag 0x80 (CRC32 u32 @8 computed over the header with the CRC field zeroed + payload; stream @12), multi-64-KiB-block streams, type 2 LZNT1 and type 3 plain LZ77 Xpress (decode rather than answering none). Name edge cases: 29-char names with no NUL inside the 60-B field, lowercase/mixed-case stored names kept verbatim, non-ASCII UTF-16. New fields: file_size_bytes (u32 @12), header_file_size_matches (bool vs decompressed length), executable_name_length, compression_format (`xpress_huffman`/`lznt1`/`xpress`/`none`), uncompressed_size_bytes (u32 @4 of MAM). Fixtures: synthesize one .pf per version + a CRC MAM from the libscca spec and assert every field.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"pcap-carryover-variants\", \"concept\": \"PCAP as a CARRIED timed family: every container the D28+ kits may mutate capture-001.pcap into\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Harden lib/meta/prebuilt/pcap.py packet_count (and every pcap field) for: pcapng (SHB 0a0d0d0a with BOM 1a2b3c4d either order, MULTIPLE sections each re-setting byte order, count EPB 6 + SPB 3 + obsolete PB 2 only -- not IDB/ISB/NRB/DSB/custom 0x0bad/0x40000bad), Kuznetzov modified pcap magic a1b2cd34 (24-B record header: +ifindex u32, protocol u16, pkt_type u8, pad), nanosecond a1b23c4d in both orders, IXIA/AIX variants (a1b2c3d4 with version 2.2/2.3), a truncated tail record (not counted, capinfos behaviour), zero-length records (counted), gzip-wrapped `.pcap.gz` (1f 8b -> decompress then parse). Fixtures: each magic x each byte order, pcapng with 2 sections + 2 IDBs, a 1-byte-short tail. Fields stay packet_count / linktype / snaplen / first/last_packet_time_utc.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"pcap-malformed-integrity\", \"concept\": \"Malformed-capture detection ('","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"persistedOutputPath":"/home/testpwn/.claude/projects/-home-testpwn-huntress-2026/4e49d64d-65c0-4a5a-ab5e-a623d76a2cdc/tool-results/bvxh1pjuz.txt","persistedOutputSize":173557},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Xxqj9wdDSNVKw9gxSF7q1z","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
